Article 9: Where the holder of land use rights, as the transferor, concludes several transfer contracts with respect to the same granted land use rights, and where the transfer contracts are valid and all transferees request performance of the contracts, the matter shall be handled separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where a transferee has gone through the procedures for registration of change of land use rights and requests the transferor to perform contractual obligations such as delivery of the land, the request shall be supported;
(2) Where none of the transferees has gone through the procedures for registration of change of land use rights, and a transferee that has first legally taken possession of the land and invested in its development requests the transferor to perform contractual obligations such as registration of change of land use rights, the request shall be supported;
(3) Where none of the transferees has gone through the procedures for registration of change of land use rights, and none has legally taken possession of the land and invested in its development, and a transferee that has first paid the land transfer price requests the transferor to perform contractual obligations such as delivery of the land and registration of change of land use rights, the request shall be supported;
(4) Where none of the contracts has been performed, and the transferee under the contract established earlier according to law requests performance of the contract, the request shall be supported.
Where a transferee that fails to obtain the land use rights requests dissolution of the contract and compensation for losses, the matter shall be handled in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Civil Code.

Article 16: Under any of the following circumstances, if a party to a contract for cooperative development of real estate requests distribution of the interests of the real estate project, the case shall not be accepted; if it has already been accepted, the prosecution shall be dismissed:
(1) a real estate construction project that requires approval according to law has not been approved by the competent department of the people's government with approval authority;
(2) the real estate construction project has not obtained a construction project planning permit;
(3) the construction project planning has been changed without authorization.
The losses caused by the parties' concealment of the fact of change to the construction project planning shall be borne by the parties according to their fault.
